  "rationale": "The added columns fail the causal-attribution test. Two of the three (department_decline_rate, is_declined) are simply the outcome restated at department and row level -- they add no cause. No TREATMENT (candidate cause whose effect on decline rate is being attributed) is supplied at all, so requirement (a) is unmet. Only department_avg_amount is a plausible non-query variable, but with no treatment present it has nothing to confound, and it is at best a weak common-cause candidate rather than part of an articulated identification strategy. There is no set-up for causal estimation: no treatment/confounder pairing that would let the department differences be attributed to an adjusted cause."
